User AI Collaboration: Read/Write Consent Policy

1. Step-by-Step Checklist for Users
	⁃	[ ] AI requests permission before performing any read/write action.
	⁃	[ ] Review the AI request for details of the intended action.
	⁃	[ ] Approve or deny the request.
	⁃	[ ] If approved, the AI performs the specified task.
	⁃	[ ] Check the activity log for all AI actions taken.
	⁃	[ ] Revoke AI consent at any time if needed.

2. Policy Document Format
Purpose
Ensure AI operates with transparency and user control for all read/write interactions.

Policy Points
	⁃	Consent Required: AI must obtain explicit user consent before any read/write action.
	⁃	Authorization Flow: Request → User Review → Approval → AI Action → Logging.
	⁃	Transparency: All actions must be logged and accessible for user review.
	⁃	Limited Access: No exploration or modification occurs without explicit approval.
	⁃	Revocation: Users can revoke consent at any time.
	⁃	Security: AI actions are sandboxed to protect the system.

Logging Requirements
	⁃	Record the date and time of each action.
	⁃	Include the description of the requested and performed action.
	⁃	Note the consent status provided by the user.

3. User Guide: How to Collaborate with AI
Step 1: Await AI Request
The AI will prompt you before attempting to read or write any files.

Step 2: Review the Request
Check the action details to understand what the AI intends to do.

Step 3: Approve or Deny
Provide explicit approval to proceed or deny to halt the action.

Step 4: Monitor Activity Logs
After approval, AI actions will be logged with timestamps and descriptions.

Step 5: Revoke Consent if Needed
At any time, you can revoke AI access, and it will immediately stop its actions.

Step 6: Example Interaction
AI: "I can organize your project folders. Do you allow me to read/write files in the Project directory?"
User: "Yes."
AI: *Action performed and logged.*
